      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Drain the soaked dried mushrooms, squeezing well. Reserve the soaking liquid. Roughly chop the mushrooms."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the oil in a large heavy-based saucepan over medium-high heat. Brown the pork belly pieces on all sides, then remove. Add the bacon and cook for 3 minutes until coloured. Remove. Brown the sausage slices for 2 minutes. Remove."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "In the same pan, cook the onion over medium heat for 8 minutes until golden. Add the tomato puree and cook for 1 minute."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the sauerkraut, fresh cabbage, mushrooms, all the browned meats, red wine, reserved mushroom soaking liquid (strain through a fine sieve), bay leaves, allspice, and peppercorns. Stir everything together."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Bring to a boil, then reduce to the lowest possible simmer. Cover and cook for 2 to 2.5 hours, stirring occasionally. The stew should be thick and the cabbage completely tender. Taste and adjust. Remove bay leaves and allspice berries before serving."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Stew is too sour"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Rinse the sauerkraut thoroughly before adding. A small pinch of sugar also helps balance the acidity."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Stew is watery"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cook uncovered for the last 20 to 30 minutes to evaporate excess liquid. Bigos should be thick and stew-like, not soupy."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Flavour is thin"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Reheat it the next day. The flavour of bigos builds significantly over 24 to 48 hours."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bigos is called the hunter's stew because it was traditionally cooked over a fire in the forest from whatever game was available. It is Poland's most famous dish and appears at every important celebration. The dish is never exactly the same twice. Every family guards their version closely."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
